 opening for a death blow  now we haven't even mentioned dodging or  anything like that  so you want to dodge when you see this  symbol pop  up this means danger in japanese  and these attacks are impossible to  block actually i shouldn't say that i  think  they're very difficult to block there  were moments in the demo where i did  block them but  i'm pretty sure it's very rare and very  difficult anyway the point of the danger  symbol  is actually that you shouldn't try to  block this and that it's much better to  try something else so if the attack is  slow then you can just interrupt it with  your own attack  and if the attack is a low sweep then  you can just jump over it  and if the attack is a thrust or  something that you think you can just  move out of the way of then you should  dash dash  is a faster version of jump but it only  gives you  horizontal spacing it doesn't put you up  in the air at all  and there's a fourth option that you  might not know about because it's pretty  rare to see in the demo  but if you're very confident that the  warning attack  is a thrust attack then you can go full  anime  and perform makiri this makiti counter  where you stamp on your enemies attack  negates the attack  it restores your posture and it can even  open your opponent  up to a death blow which makes it  probably the highest skill cap  thing you can do in sikiro i think  because  it's pretty dangerous to dodge into an  attack especially if you're not sure  if it's a thrust and even more  interestingly  in our interview yasuhiro mentioned that  makidi was an unlockable skill  which leads me to believe that there  might actually be other types of counter  available which is really cool  i actually see a lot of people  criticizing the idea of a warning attack  because they think it's hand-holding or  they think it's going to make the game  more accessible  but they're wrong because warning  attacks aren't just telling you to do  one thing they're not just saying hey an  attack is coming  you need to dodge they're actually  telling you hey there's a dangerous  attack coming  and you need to decide whether you're  going to counter-attack  counter with mckitty dash or jump  and that's entirely up to your reflexes  and having the warning symbol show up at  all  actually enables your reflexes to act  even faster  and helps with decision making and i  know not everyone defines combat in this  way but  i would define good combat as enabling  the player to  make multiple effective decisions over a  short period of time  and the warning symbol system actually  tells you that there's a complex  decision to be made  not the opposite and it actually enables  the complex combat of sikiro to flow  so fast the best example of good combat  in the demo  is the samurai general who you're  probably getting pretty sick of seeing  by this point he has it all though he  has two health bars he has  insane attack variety he has hyper armor  attacks he has  charged attacks numerous warning  abilities  and he's even got this special move that  replenishes all his posture which might  actually be an unlockable skill for our  character hopefully  the samurai general like the chained  ogre is  a mid-boss a sort of mini boss that from  software says that we can expect to see  more of  in sikhiro and in their level design and  i really liked it because the ogre and  the samurai general and  the other secret hidden enemy i'm not  allowed to talk about  they made the levels like really  memorable and i think it's way more  memorable than fighting a bunch of  smaller enemies  another thing that made the levels  really memorable was the music  so one of the best things about souls i  always thought  was how melancholy and quiet  the overworld is i actually love the  ambient noise in souls games  so at first i was kind of skeptical of  sakiro  because there's this mid-level music  but i have to say it's grown on me when  you're out of combat  the music is quiet and brooding but  as soon as combat begins it's drums  wind flutes and vocals all beating to  the sound of swords clashing  and blood spraying it suits sakiro's  faster combat  and in addition to that it actually  serves a bit of a purpose because  when you're sneaking around it's really  quiet but then as soon as you get  spotted  the action music kicks in and it breaks  the tension  and the calm of stealth in terms of  criticism  there really isn't too much i can say  because it's all subject to change  but here is my feedback so far so first  the ui now from software's uis in demos  always change and i think it's fair to  say that this one has to change a little  bit too  i found it a little bit strange that  health is off to the left  for our character and for enemies  especially since  health is actually linked to posture so  in my opinion it would make a bit more  sense if  health and posture were linked and  represented in the middle of the screen  or something like that although i'm not  a ui expert  i want to say that healing was really  annoying in the demo because it's bound  to  up on the d-pad with item use and up on  the d-pad is a really annoying button to  press while you're trying to move  with the left thumb stick it's a bit  easier on a ps4 controller but it's  quite difficult on an xbox controller i  found  but sikiro has a ton of new inputs  there's  jump there's eavesdrop you have to cycle  through your prosthetic weapons  so it's not really a surprise that they  had to put healing  on the d-pad but we'll see how that goes  um third when you fall off a cliff  insecure you actually don't die you  don't even  necessarily lose a life you actually  just take damage  from falling off a cliff and i don't  think i'm a fan of that  it's already pretty difficult to fall  off cliffs in sikiro  because your character actually just  sticks to the edge of platforms he  doesn't just fall off  so it's hard to fall off and i think you  should actually  lose a life if you fall off because that  way  there's less teleportation there's more  tension and  when you jump off the bridge during the  boss fight which happened to me twice  you should still get a second chance i  think just losing health is a little bit  too  generous the difficulty is on point  though  don't you worry about that if you think  it's too easy  that's because i'm biased and i'm  probably not showing you  all the times that i played really badly  and to be honest  you haven't seen the rest of the demo  the boss is hard the optional enemy in  the demo  is really hard and i only beat  both of these enemies once and that was  because i had hours  with the game only a few people defeated  the boss at gamescom  and i only heard of one other person who  defeated  the headless enemy and i asked around a  fair bit  so yeah it's fair it's full of secrets  and  the game is tough as nails so don't  worry  but again if you ever find a convention  that has this demo  available go there line up play it  because can you tell i adore this game i  really do  like you guys know that i get excited  for every new from software game  and that i am biased and it is my job  and everything right but  honestly sakiro is a little bit  different than usual because  every souls game evolves every souls  game adds new  things right but sequito is the first  from software game that i've played that  is actually  replacing things it's actually cutting  parts out of the salt's formula  that people love they're taking risks  and  they're making a lot of plebs upset and  basically  they're cutting off a perfectly  functional arm and they're replacing it  with  something they think is even better see  if you can spot the metaphor  uh it's risky it's new but whatever  they're doing  it is working 100 it is absolutely  working and  i think that's part of the biggest  reason why this feels like the biggest  evolution of souls combat to date  you're gonna have to excuse my gushing  for a little bit longer  it was actually really cool to be at  gamescom because i got to hear from a  couple of folks at activision who had  never really played  a souls game before and you could tell  they were starting to figure out  why from software's games are so special  and i love that  helping people see why from software's  games are so great  is literally at the core of why i even  make  videos right so i got such a kick out of  going to gamescom  and seeing that joy anyway that's enough  of sikiro  until tokyo game show most likely uh  i'll be making videos of that as soon as  i can so subscribe  if you're interested in finally seeing  the monk boss  and if you're a patron i'll be uploading  the raw uncompressed footage  for you guys whether it's gamescom or  tokyo game show in a month or so  that's as a reward for supporting the  channel so thank you very much  and until next time guys i'll see you  later
 

